.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH CSPLIT 1 "2026-09-01"
.SH "نام (NAME)"
csplit \- Split a file into sections determined by context lines
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
\fBcsplit\fR [OPTION]... FILE PATTERN...
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
Split a file into sections determined by context lines
.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.TP
\fB\-b\fR, \fB\-\-suffix\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR
use sprintf FORMAT instead of %02d
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-prefix\fR \fI<PREFIX>\fR
use PREFIX instead of \*(Aqxx\*(Aq
.TP
\fB\-k\fR, \fB\-\-keep\-files\fR
do not remove output files on errors
.TP
\fB\-\-suppress\-matched\fR
suppress the lines matching PATTERN
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-digits\fR \fI<DIGITS>\fR
use specified number of digits instead of 2
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
do not print counts of output file sizes
.TP
\fB\-z\fR, \fB\-\-elide\-empty\-files\fR
remove empty output files
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH EXTRA
Output pieces of FILE separated by PATTERN(s) to files \*(Aqxx00\*(Aq, \*(Aqxx01\*(Aq, ..., and output byte counts of each piece to standard output.
.SH "نسخه (VERSION)"
v(uutils coreutils) 0.11.0
